ng why then your business is dead  in the water so make sure you  send yourself around that every time you  feeling low the second thing is it was  surround myself with entrepreneurial  mentors who I looked up to and looked at  their early years look at their early  stories because any successful  entrepreneur that you would look up to  they had they struggled early on it  wasn't just handed to them they had  setbacks they had failures they probably  started with less than what you already  have right now and just realizing that  gave me the motivation to keep going  that if Bill Gates could do this if  Oprah Winfrey could do this if Steve  Jobs could do this and if these people  who didn't have a lot could go and make  something of themselves and become  massively successful then I can do it  too  so remembering the why I'm focusing on  success stories that really with  motivation on a daily basis I found  helped me stay motivated but it's got to  be something that you still believe in  and don't give up because you're afraid  so the question day today is when did  you consider giving up what are the  reasons behind it going a little deep  little personal leaving comments below  I'm going to join the discussion I also  want to give a quick shout out to  William Chilton William thank you so  much for buying a copy my book really  means a lot to me  those are you watching if you want to  change that a shadow in a future video  make sure to grab a copy of the book and  email in your receipt so we can keep  track thank you guys so much for  watching have an amazing day you seem to  believe or whatever your one word is and  I'll see you again tomorrow morning for  another shot of an espresso  you
 

